{"id":"b474aed7bc1f8c495892cd5699e3db42f611687a","axis":"silent","repo":"phpstan/phpstan","sha":"b474aed7bc1f8c495892cd5699e3db42f611687a","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"website/CLAUDE.md","lines":["@@ -59,7 +59,8 @@ Built on GitHub Actions, deployed to AWS S3 (`web-phpstan.org` bucket) with Clou"," "," Interactive UI is written as TSX in `src/js/*.tsx` and rendered by TKO's `@tko/build.reference` (`ko.jsx`), never as `data-bind` strings in Nunjucks:"," ","-- Nunjucks renders an empty placeholder element; `mount(id, template)` from `src/js/tsx.ts` replaces it with the rendered template and applies its bindings. Never apply bindings to the whole page: `@tko/build.reference` would turn `{{ … }}` in documentation text into bindings.","+- Each widget is a component: a `ko.Component` subclass that is its own view model, with a `get template()` returning TSX and a `static override readonly customElementName` (set it explicitly: minification renames classes). Subscribe with `this.subscribe(observable, callback)` and create computeds that read other components' state with `this.computed()`, so they are disposed with the component; `koDescendantsComplete()` runs once the template is in the document. Large view models keep the template in a function in a separate `.tsx` file (`PlaygroundViewModel` → `playgroundTemplate()` in `Playground.tsx`).","+- Nunjucks renders a placeholder element; `mountComponent(id, Component, params)` from `src/js/tsx.ts` replaces it with the component (the placeholder stays if the constructor throws). `mount(id, template)` does the same for a template without its own state. Never apply bindings to the whole page: `@tko/build.reference` would turn `{{ … }}` in documentation text into bindings."," - Bindings are `ko-*` attributes whose values are TypeScript expressions, e.g. `ko-text={vm.title}`, `ko-click={() => vm.save()}`. Pass observables, not their values; derived values need a `ko.pureComputed`. Use `when(condition, template)` for conditional parts and a `ko.pureComputed` that maps an array for lists."," - `src/js/jsx.d.ts` types the allowed attributes and bindings, so `npm run check` (tsc) rejects wrong values; the `tko/known-bindings` ESLint rule rejects misspelled binding names. Custom binding handlers declare their binding by augmenting `KoCustomBindings`."," - Server-rendered content that only needs to be shown or hidden (the sidebar, the mobile menu) stays in Nunjucks and gets typed bindings through `bindElement(id, bindings)`."],"additions":2,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"website/src/js/ErrorIdentifierSearch.tsx","lines":["@@ -1,29 +1,145 @@"," import ko from '@tko/build.reference';","-import {ErrorIdentifierSearchViewModel} from './ErrorIdentifierSearchViewModel';","-import {mount, when} from './tsx';","+import {when} from './tsx';","+","+declare const __ERRORS_IDENTIFIERS_JSON__: Record<string, Record<string, Record<string, string[]>>>;","+declare const __EXCLUDED_ERROR_IDENTIFIERS_JSON__: string[];","+","+interface SearchResult {","+\tidentifier: string;","+\tlink: string;","+}","+","+const allIdentifiers = Object.keys(__ERRORS_IDENTIFIERS_JSON__).sort();","+","+function searchResult(identifier: string): SearchResult {","+\treturn {identifier, link: `/error-identifiers/${identifier}`};","+}"," "," // The search box and random examples shown on /documentation and /error-identifiers.","-export function initErrorIdentifierSearch(examplesTarget?: string): void {","-\tconst search = new ErrorIdentifierSearchViewModel();","-","-\tmount('identifier-search-widget', (","-\t\t<div>","-\t\t\t<div class=\"relative max-w-md\">","-\t\t\t\t<input id=\"identifier-search\" type=\"text\" class=\"w-full px-4 py-3 border-2 border-gray-300 rounded-lg text-sm font-mono focus:border-blue-500 focus:outline-none transition duration-150\" placeholder=\"e.g. argument.type, return.missing, deadCode...\" ko-textInput={search.query} ko-event={{keydown: search.onKeyDown, focus: search.onFocus, blur: search.onBlur}} au